# Git attribution and push policy

## Never push unless asked

- Do **not** run `git push` (or `git push -u`) unless the user explicitly asks in that message.
- Do **not** publish to npm unless the user explicitly asks.
- Committing locally is fine when the user asks for a commit; pushing is a separate explicit request.

## Author must be nitsan-ai only

- Repo commits must show **NITSAN AI / nitsan-ai** only — never **cursoragent** / Cursor as co-author on GitHub.
- After every `git commit`, check the message body. If it contains `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or `cursoragent@cursor.com`, remove that trailer immediately with a **new** commit rewrite only when safe:
  - If the commit was **just created by you** in this turn, **not pushed**, amend once to strip the trailer (user rules amend conditions apply).
  - Prefer preventing the trailer via `.githooks/commit-msg` (strip Cursor co-authors).
- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `cursoragent` yourself.
- Do not change `git config` user.name / user.email.

## Enable the hook (once per clone)

```bash
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
```

(Only the human should run that if agents must not update git config; if hooksPath is already set, rely on it.)
